// createPreNeedDealFromContact (ZP-TBD-68 -- Pre-Need from Contact)
// ============================================================================
// NEW standalone CRM function. Called from the preNeedFromContactWidget
// (D:\Office\Andrea_Projects\DFH\widgets\preNeedFromContact\preNeedFromContactWidget)
// via ZOHO.CRM.FUNCTIONS.execute("createpreneeddealfromcontact", ...), which
// is triggered by a new "Create Pre-Need Deal" Widget-type custom button on
// the Contacts module.
//
// SOURCE: task6.txt (D:\Office\Andrea_Projects\DFH\projectDocuments\), which
// explicitly says the existing Lead-conversion logic in
// convertLeadOnChangingLeadStatus should be LIFTED, not rewritten. Pulled
// that function's live source 2026-09-16 before writing anything here (its
// full code and analysis are further down in this file, for reference).
//
// T-07 (task7.txt, same folder): every Contact this function creates or
// touches must get a valid Contacts.Contact_Type. Confirmed live 2026-09-16
// via ZohoCRM_getFields: Contact_Type is a picklist, currently valid values
// are -None-/Deceased Contact/IFR/Guarantor/JTB Rep/Tour Rep/Forensics
// Lab/Police/Hospital/Funeral Home/Driver/Doctor/Attendant/Portal
// User/On Scene Contact/Investigating Officer/Amber Driver (unused) -- no
// payer value exists yet. Confirmed with the developer: add a new value
// "Payer" (manual Setup step, no write API for CRM picklist values from this
// session -- see metadata.md). This function now sets:
//   - payer Contact  -> Contact_Type = "Payer"  (both scenarios)
//   - beneficiary Contact -> Contact_Type = "IFR" (Scenario 2 only; in
//     Scenario 1 the payer IS the beneficiary and keeps "Payer" -- she only
//     ever gets the "Primary Contact" Deal role below, never "IFR", so
//     Contact_Type mirrors that)
// enforced at the function level only (not as a layout-level required
// field), since a layout-level requirement would be global and break every
// other Contact-creation path in the org (NOKIntake, Lead conversion, manual
// CRM entry, MNSJ setup, etc.) that doesn't set Contact_Type today.
// Explicitly does NOT use Is_this_Contact_IFR for this -- task7.txt calls
// out that having both fields represent the same thing risks them
// disagreeing; Contact_Type is the single source of truth going forward.
// Also explicitly does NOT copy the confirmed live bug in
// convertLeadOnChangingLeadStatus, which does
// intendedFuneralReciepent.put("Contact_Type",ifnull(recordInfo.get("Pre_Need_Contact_Role"),""))
// -- Pre_Need_Contact_Role holds answers like "For Self"/"For Spouse"/"For
// Family Member", which are not valid Contact_Type picklist values at all.
// That bug is left as-is in the old (soon-to-be-retired) Lead function --
// fixing it wasn't asked for and is a separate call for Andrea/Dale once the
// Lead flow's retirement is decided.
//
// DUPLICATE DETECTION (added 2026-09-16 after live testing of TC-07 showed
// re-running the same beneficiary created a brand-new Account every time):
// before creating the beneficiary Account, search Accounts by exact
// Account_Name + Account_Type=Deceased and reuse a match instead of
// creating another one (mirrors convertLeadOnChangingLeadStatus's own
// search-then-create pattern for its IFR Account). Same idea for the
// beneficiary Contact in Scenario 2 -- if the Account was reused, search
// Contacts already linked to that Account (Account_Name = accountId) before
// creating a new one. A fresh Account never matches, so this only changes
// behavior on true re-runs with the same beneficiary. Contact_Type is set
// via an explicit updateRecord after resolving the Contact either way, so a
// reused older Contact still ends up correct even if it predates T-07.
//
// WHAT'S REUSED FROM convertLeadOnChangingLeadStatus, AS-IS:
// - The Contact_Roles PUT mechanism: PUT /crm/v6/Deals/{dealId}/Contact_Roles/{contactId}
//   with a {"data":[{"Contact_Role":{"name":...,"id":...}}]} body.
// - The "Primary Contact" role id, 6503357000001327140 -- hardcoded in the
//   live function today, reused as-is since it's already proven working.
// - The dynamic "look up or create" pattern for a Contact Role master record
//   via POST/GET /crm/v7/Contacts/roles, including the DUPLICATE_DATA
//   fallback (create returns DUPLICATE_DATA if the role name already
//   exists -- the code then re-fetches the full list to find its id).
//
// WHAT'S DELIBERATELY NOT REUSED (per the brief and live-code review):
// 1. THE KNOWN BUG the brief calls out: the old function does
//        accountMap.put("Account_Type","IFR");
//        ... (many other fields) ...
//        accountMap.put("Account_Type",ifnull(recordInfo.get("Account_Type"),""));
//    -- the second line overwrites the first with a blank, since Leads
//    don't have an Account_Type field. This function sets Account_Type to
//    "Deceased" exactly ONCE and never touches it again.
// 2. The old function also reassigns the (freshly-converted-from-Lead)
//    Contact's own Account_Name to the newly-created IFR Account:
//        contactMap.put("Account_Name",accountId);
//        zoho.crm.updateRecord("Contacts",contactId,contactMap,...);
//    That's harmless in the old Lead-conversion context (the Contact was
//    created seconds earlier with no prior Account). In this new flow the
//    payer is a pre-existing real Contact who may already belong to their
//    own Account -- reassigning it to the beneficiary's Account would
//    silently break that. Confirmed with the developer 2026-09-16: do NOT
//    do this. The payer Contact's own Account_Name is left untouched.
//
// PREREQUISITES (manual setup, no write API available to this session for
// either CRM custom fields or CRM functions -- see guideline.md):
// - New Accounts custom field for TRN. Suggested api_name: Deceased_TRN
//   (Text, single line), alongside the existing Deceased_* fields. NOT YET
//   CREATED as of this writing -- the accountMap.put("Deceased_TRN", ...)
//   line below uses that name as a placeholder; correct it once the field
//   actually exists and its live api_name is confirmed (same lesson as
//   ZP-TBD-65's cf_xero_retainer_credit_note_id: don't assume a guessed
//   name is right, verify it).
// - This function itself needs to be created in CRM Setup > Developer
//   Space > Functions as a Standalone function, return type String.
// - A new "Create Pre-Need Deal" custom button on the Contacts module,
//   type Widget, pointing at the deployed preNeedFromContactWidget.
//
// CONFIRMED LIVE (2026-09-16) before building any of this:
// - Deals.Pipeline value for Pre Need is literally the string "Pre Need"
//   (both display_value and actual_value) -- no numeric pipeline id needed.
//   The old function has a commented-out numeric Pipeline id
//   ("6049981000002144040") that looks like a stale/wrong leftover; not
//   reused here.
// - Initial Stage for a freshly created Pre-Need Deal: "Qualification"
//   (displayed as "Requested" -- the first stage in the Pre Need pipeline),
//   per the developer's explicit choice.
// - Contacts module already has all the standard fields this function needs
//   for the beneficiary Contact (First_Name, Last_Name, Date_of_Birth,
//   Email, Phone, Mailing_Street/City/State/Zip/Country, Account_Name) --
//   confirmed via ZohoCRM_getFields, nothing missing there.

string standalone.createPreNeedDealFromContact(String payerContactId, String isPayerSame, String beneficiaryFirstName, String beneficiaryLastName, String beneficiaryDOB, String beneficiaryStreet, String beneficiaryStreet2, String beneficiaryCity, String beneficiaryState, String beneficiaryZip, String beneficiaryCountry, String beneficiaryPhone, String beneficiaryEmail, String beneficiaryTRN)
{
	resultMap = Map();
	try
	{
		payerContact = zoho.crm.getRecordById("Contacts",payerContactId);
		if(isNull(payerContact))
		{
			resultMap.put("status","error");
			resultMap.put("message","Payer contact not found: " + payerContactId);
			return resultMap.toString();
		}

		beneficiaryFullName = beneficiaryFirstName + " " + beneficiaryLastName;

		// ==========================================
		// BUILD THE DECEASED/BENEFICIARY ACCOUNT
		// Account_Type set ONCE, hardcoded "Deceased" -- see note 1 above,
		// this is the exact bug the brief warned against.
		// ==========================================
		accountMap = Map();
		accountMap.put("Account_Name",beneficiaryFullName);
		accountMap.put("Account_Type","Deceased");
		accountMap.put("Deceased_First_Name",beneficiaryFirstName);
		accountMap.put("Deceased_Last_Name",beneficiaryLastName);
		if(!isNull(beneficiaryDOB) && beneficiaryDOB != "")
		{
			accountMap.put("Date_of_Birth",beneficiaryDOB);
		}
		accountMap.put("Deceased_Street_Address",ifnull(beneficiaryStreet,""));
		accountMap.put("Deceased_Street_Address_2",ifnull(beneficiaryStreet2,""));
		accountMap.put("Deceased_City",ifnull(beneficiaryCity,""));
		accountMap.put("Deceased_State",ifnull(beneficiaryState,""));
		accountMap.put("Deceased_Zip_Code",ifnull(beneficiaryZip,""));
		accountMap.put("Deceased_Country",ifnull(beneficiaryCountry,""));
		accountMap.put("Phone",ifnull(beneficiaryPhone,""));
		accountMap.put("Email",ifnull(beneficiaryEmail,""));
		// TODO: confirm the live api_name once the TRN field is created on
		// Accounts -- "Deceased_TRN" is a placeholder, not yet verified.
		accountMap.put("Deceased_TRN",ifnull(beneficiaryTRN,""));

		// DUPLICATE DETECTION (added on request, after live testing showed
		// re-running the same beneficiary created a fresh Account every
		// time): search for an existing Deceased Account with this exact
		// name before creating a new one, mirroring the search-then-create
		// pattern convertLeadOnChangingLeadStatus already uses for its IFR
		// Account. If found, reuse it as-is (not updated) rather than
		// overwriting whatever's already there.
		accountSearchQuery = Map();
		accountSearchQuery.put("select_query","select id from Accounts where Account_Name = '" + beneficiaryFullName + "' and Account_Type = 'Deceased' limit 1");
		accountSearchResponse = invokeurl
		[
			url :"https://www.zohoapis.com/crm/v7/coql"
			type :POST
			parameters:accountSearchQuery.toString()
			connection:"zohooauth"
		];
		if(!isNull(accountSearchResponse.get("data")) && accountSearchResponse.get("data").size() > 0)
		{
			accountId = accountSearchResponse.get("data").get(0).get("id");
		}
		else
		{
			accountResult = zoho.crm.createRecord("Accounts",accountMap);
			if(isNull(accountResult.get("id")))
			{
				resultMap.put("status","error");
				resultMap.put("message","Account creation failed: " + accountResult.toString());
				return resultMap.toString();
			}
			accountId = accountResult.get("id");
		}

		// ==========================================
		// DETERMINE THE BENEFICIARY CONTACT
		// ==========================================
		if(isPayerSame == "true")
		{
			// Scenario 1: payer and beneficiary are the same person --
			// reuse the existing payer Contact, no new Contact needed.
			beneficiaryContactId = payerContactId;

			// Link this Contact to the new Account. Unlike Scenario 2
			// (different payer/beneficiary, see the "else" branch and the
			// design note near the top of this file), there is no risk of
			// clobbering an unrelated existing Account relationship here --
			// the Account being linked genuinely IS this same person's own
			// record, since they are the beneficiary too. Confirmed as a
			// gap via live testing 2026-09-16: without this, the new
			// Account was created but never showed up on the Contact.
			// T-07: payer's Contact_Type must be set explicitly, not left
			// blank and not inferred from Is_this_Contact_IFR. Mary only
			// ever gets the "Primary Contact" role on the Deal below (never
			// "IFR", even here where she's also the beneficiary) --
			// Contact_Type mirrors that same Payer role.
			selfAccountLinkMap = Map();
			selfAccountLinkMap.put("Account_Name",accountId);
			selfAccountLinkMap.put("Contact_Type","Payer");
			zoho.crm.updateRecord("Contacts",payerContactId,selfAccountLinkMap);
		}
		else
		{
			// Scenario 2: create a NEW Contact for the beneficiary, linked
			// to the Account just created above.
			beneficiaryContactMap = Map();
			beneficiaryContactMap.put("First_Name",beneficiaryFirstName);
			beneficiaryContactMap.put("Last_Name",beneficiaryLastName);
			if(!isNull(beneficiaryDOB) && beneficiaryDOB != "")
			{
				beneficiaryContactMap.put("Date_of_Birth",beneficiaryDOB);
			}
			beneficiaryContactMap.put("Mailing_Street",ifnull(beneficiaryStreet,""));
			beneficiaryContactMap.put("Mailing_Street_2",ifnull(beneficiaryStreet2,""));
			beneficiaryContactMap.put("Mailing_City",ifnull(beneficiaryCity,""));
			beneficiaryContactMap.put("Mailing_State",ifnull(beneficiaryState,""));
			beneficiaryContactMap.put("Mailing_Zip",ifnull(beneficiaryZip,""));
			beneficiaryContactMap.put("Mailing_Country",ifnull(beneficiaryCountry,""));
			beneficiaryContactMap.put("Phone",ifnull(beneficiaryPhone,""));
			beneficiaryContactMap.put("Email",ifnull(beneficiaryEmail,""));
			beneficiaryContactMap.put("Account_Name",accountId);

			// DUPLICATE DETECTION (added on request): if the Account above
			// was reused rather than freshly created, it may already have a
			// beneficiary Contact linked to it from an earlier run -- reuse
			// that Contact instead of creating another one on the same
			// Account. A fresh Account (just created above) will never
			// match here, so this only fires on true re-runs.
			contactSearchQuery = Map();
			contactSearchQuery.put("select_query","select id from Contacts where Account_Name = '" + accountId + "' limit 1");
			contactSearchResponse = invokeurl
			[
				url :"https://www.zohoapis.com/crm/v7/coql"
				type :POST
				parameters:contactSearchQuery.toString()
				connection:"zohooauth"
			];
			if(!isNull(contactSearchResponse.get("data")) && contactSearchResponse.get("data").size() > 0)
			{
				beneficiaryContactId = contactSearchResponse.get("data").get(0).get("id");
			}
			else
			{
				beneficiaryContactResult = zoho.crm.createRecord("Contacts",beneficiaryContactMap);
				if(isNull(beneficiaryContactResult.get("id")))
				{
					resultMap.put("status","error");
					resultMap.put("message","Beneficiary contact creation failed: " + beneficiaryContactResult.toString());
					return resultMap.toString();
				}
				beneficiaryContactId = beneficiaryContactResult.get("id");
			}

			// T-07: beneficiary Contact_Type = "IFR" -- the actual role
			// value, not the Pre_Need_Contact_Role answer ("For Self"/"For
			// Spouse"/"For Family Member") that convertLeadOnChangingLeadStatus
			// wrongly writes into this same field. Set unconditionally here
			// (not just in beneficiaryContactMap above) so a reused Contact
			// from an older run still ends up correct, not just a freshly
			// created one.
			beneficiaryContactTypeMap = Map();
			beneficiaryContactTypeMap.put("Contact_Type","IFR");
			zoho.crm.updateRecord("Contacts",beneficiaryContactId,beneficiaryContactTypeMap);

			// T-07: set the (pre-existing) payer's Contact_Type too, without
			// touching Account_Name -- that field is deliberately left alone
			// for the payer in this scenario (see the design note near the
			// top of this file: reassigning the payer's own Account to the
			// beneficiary's Account would silently break their real Account
			// relationship).
			payerContactTypeMap = Map();
			payerContactTypeMap.put("Contact_Type","Payer");
			zoho.crm.updateRecord("Contacts",payerContactId,payerContactTypeMap);
		}

		// ==========================================
		// CREATE THE PRE-NEED DEAL
		// Account = beneficiary. Contact_Name = the PAYER, always.
		// Per the brief: "Contact = who pays; Account = who the funeral is
		// for" -- and once set, the Account must not change later, since
		// the Books retainer connects to the Deal's Account.
		// ==========================================
		// SWITCHED TO RAW REST (invokeurl POST /crm/v7/Deals) -- confirmed
		// live 2026-09-16 that the native zoho.crm.createRecord("Deals",...)
		// task gives inconsistent Pipeline/Layout/Stage behavior for this
		// module: even with the numerically-correct Pipeline id
		// (6503357000001556214, confirmed via ZohoCRM_getPipelines to
		// genuinely be "Pre Need" on this exact layout), the created Deal's
		// Pipeline still resolved to "Standard (Standard)" -- the module's
		// default pipeline -- instead. Found a directly comparable, already
		// proven-working example instead:
		// crm/functions/deals/ZP-TBD-8_police_dropoff_workflow/createOnePoliceDropoffDeceased.deluge
		// creates Deals via this exact raw REST endpoint, on this SAME
		// Layout id, with Pipeline/Stage/Type as LABEL strings (not numeric
		// ids) -- e.g. dealMap.put("Pipeline","Police Cases"). Mirroring
		// that exactly here rather than trusting the native task's field
		// coercion, which behaves differently (and, per this ticket's own
		// testing, unreliably) from raw REST for this field combination.
		dealAccountMap = Map();
		dealAccountMap.put("id",accountId);
		dealContactMap = Map();
		dealContactMap.put("id",payerContactId);

		dealMap = Map();
		dealMap.put("Deal_Name",beneficiaryFullName);
		dealMap.put("Name_of_Deceased",beneficiaryFullName);
		dealMap.put("Layout","6503357000000091023");
		dealMap.put("Pipeline","Pre Need");
		dealMap.put("Stage","Requested");
		dealMap.put("Type","Pre Need");
		dealMap.put("Account_Name",dealAccountMap);
		dealMap.put("Contact_Name",dealContactMap);

		dealList = list();
		dealList.add(dealMap);
		dealContainer = Map();
		dealContainer.put("data",dealList);

		createDealResponse = invokeurl
		[
			url :"https://www.zohoapis.com/crm/v7/Deals"
			type :POST
			parameters:dealContainer.toString()
			connection:"zohooauth"
		];

		dealCreateResult = createDealResponse.get("data").get(0);
		if(dealCreateResult.get("code") != "SUCCESS")
		{
			resultMap.put("status","error");
			resultMap.put("message","Deal creation failed: " + createDealResponse.toString());
			return resultMap.toString();
		}
		dealId = dealCreateResult.get("details").get("id");

		// ==========================================
		// ASSIGN CONTACT ROLES ON THE DEAL
		// Reuses the exact PUT /Contact_Roles/{contactId} mechanism already
		// proven in convertLeadOnChangingLeadStatus.
		// ==========================================
		primaryContactList = list();
		primaryContactMap = Map();
		primaryContactMap.put("name","Primary Contact");
		primaryContactMap.put("id","6503357000001327140");
		primaryContactRoleMap = Map();
		primaryContactRoleMap.put("Contact_Role",primaryContactMap);
		primaryContactList.add(primaryContactRoleMap);
		primaryContactListRoleData = Map();
		primaryContactListRoleData.put("data",primaryContactList);
		assignPrimaryContactRole = invokeurl
		[
			url :"https://www.zohoapis.com/crm/v6/Deals/" + dealId + "/Contact_Roles/" + payerContactId
			type :PUT
			parameters:primaryContactListRoleData.toString()
			connection:"zohooauth"
		];

		if(isPayerSame != "true")
		{
			// Look up (or create, if it doesn't already exist) the "IFR"
			// Contact Role master record -- same dynamic lookup-or-create
			// + DUPLICATE_DATA handling already proven in
			// convertLeadOnChangingLeadStatus.
			ifrRoleId = null;
			contactRoleNameList = list();
			contactRole = Map();
			contactRole.put("name","IFR");
			contactRoleNameList.add(contactRole);
			contactRoleNameMap = Map();
			contactRoleNameMap.put("contact_roles",contactRoleNameList);
			createNewRoleName = invokeurl
			[
				url :"https://www.zohoapis.com/crm/v7/Contacts/roles"
				type :POST
				parameters:contactRoleNameMap.toString()
				connection:"zohooauth"
			];
			for each  contactRoleInfo in createNewRoleName.get("contact_roles")
			{
				if(contactRoleInfo.get("code") == "DUPLICATE_DATA")
				{
					allContactRoles = invokeurl
					[
						url :"https://www.zohoapis.com/crm/v7/Contacts/roles"
						type :GET
						connection:"zohooauth"
					];
					for each  singleContactRole in allContactRoles.get("contact_roles")
					{
						if(singleContactRole.get("name") == "IFR")
						{
							ifrRoleId = singleContactRole.get("id");
						}
					}
				}
				else if(contactRoleInfo.get("code") == "SUCCESS")
				{
					ifrRoleId = contactRoleInfo.get("details").get("id");
				}
			}
			ifrRoleList = list();
			ifrRoleMap = Map();
			ifrRoleMap.put("name","IFR");
			ifrRoleMap.put("id",ifrRoleId);
			ifrContactRoleMap = Map();
			ifrContactRoleMap.put("Contact_Role",ifrRoleMap);
			ifrRoleList.add(ifrContactRoleMap);
			ifrRoleData = Map();
			ifrRoleData.put("data",ifrRoleList);
			assignIfrRole = invokeurl
			[
				url :"https://www.zohoapis.com/crm/v6/Deals/" + dealId + "/Contact_Roles/" + beneficiaryContactId
				type :PUT
				parameters:ifrRoleData.toString()
				connection:"zohooauth"
			];
		}

		resultMap.put("status","success");
		resultMap.put("dealId",dealId);
		resultMap.put("accountId",accountId);
		resultMap.put("beneficiaryContactId",beneficiaryContactId);
		return resultMap.toString();
	}
	catch (e)
	{
		resultMap.put("status","error");
		resultMap.put("message",e.toString());
		return resultMap.toString();
	}
}
